WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.020
- It's time to wash the floofy newfie.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.933
Bear, get in here.

00:00:05.933 --> 00:00:07.370
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.780
Newf, hi puppy.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.280
So this is one of the
Bengal Newfoundlands.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.360
I'm trying to be like that guy

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.087
that shows the cats on the TikTok.

00:00:18.087 --> 00:00:19.260
Oh, he's too heavy.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.190
Okay, you ready?

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.180
It's bath time.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.013
You're stinky.

00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:23.850
I took you out in the rain.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.200
You were running around the field.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.463
Let's go in, bath time.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.103
Excellent job.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.680
Bear's really easy

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.260
to wash actually, 'cause he's
just like down for anything.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.700
But I like to tell him like I do

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.740
with my patients, all
the things I'm gonna do

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:38.610
before I do them.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.190
So Bear, the first thing I'm
gonna do is turn on the water.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.270
Then I'm gonna wet you.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.560
I'm gonna get you very wet.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.720
Then once that happens,
I'm gonna get the shampoo

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:46.890
and I'm gonna lather you up.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:48.090
Once you're fully lathered,

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.700
I'm gonna make sure I get
all ends washed of you,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.110
from top to bottom.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:52.943
Do you agree?

00:00:52.943 --> 00:00:53.856
High-five if you agree.

00:00:53.856 --> 00:00:54.689
(paw smacking)

00:00:54.689 --> 00:00:55.522
Okay, you agree, good.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:56.700
The problem with this water is

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.610
sometimes it has really bad
control over temperature.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.310
So I wanna make sure
that it's not too hot.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.620
'Cause for dogs, hot water is no bueno.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.480
The craziest thing about Bear is

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.880
that he looks huge when he's all poofy,

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.850
but when he starts getting wet,
he's actually really skinny.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.860
Bear, how you feeling about this?

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.150
His fur is actually a
little oily, the top layer.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.400
So it prevents water from getting in.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.890
Bear, can I have a kiss while I wash you?

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:23.836
Thank you.

00:01:23.836 --> 00:01:24.669
(Mike grunting)

00:01:24.669 --> 00:01:27.300
So you gotta be careful when
you get dog shampoo like I did.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.580
I got the one that's concentrated,

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.980
so you're gonna need to
dilute it pretty heavily.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.562
Bear, this is your shampoo.

00:01:33.562 --> 00:01:34.485
(shampoo gurgling)

00:01:34.485 --> 00:01:36.185
All right, newfie.

00:01:36.185 --> 00:01:38.550
(water splashing)

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:39.750
Oh, it's so heavy.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.300
This is the version of a dog sponge.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.200
So you wanna introduce it

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.620
to the dog so he feels safe
with it, lets him smell it.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:47.970
I mean Bear's really laid back

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.580
so it doesn't matter at all,
what you do with him, but.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.920
Okay, now we wash the newf,

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.770
make sure we get deep into his skin folds.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.770
The good part about this rubbery
thing is it does a good job

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.179
of getting through the fur even the knots.

00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:02.460
(water splashing)

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.870
Also, when you do this with your dog

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:04.830
it should be a fun thing.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:06.780
So bringing your dog snacks is great.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.460
Bear, do you want a snack?

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.720
Or do you wanna just lick my face?

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.770
Your breath's gonna smell better

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.060
after I brush your teeth though.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:14.679
Look how much fur comes out of this guy.

00:02:14.679 --> 00:02:16.054
(air whooshing)

00:02:16.054 --> 00:02:17.100
Ugh!

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.420
Bear, I feel like you're concentrating

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.830
on solving a math problem.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.690
Which math problem are you thinking about?

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.670
Clean the butt, he doesn't like that.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.830
Good boy, Bear, good boy.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.720
Oh my God, look at this.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.353
(audience gasping)

00:02:29.353 --> 00:02:32.760
I have a special
ShamWow-esque product here

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.580
where you can actually put
your hands inside of this,

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.610
and just hug your dog like
it's a giant little loofah.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:39.900
Giant little loofah.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.099
Look, it's like he's being born.

00:02:41.099 --> 00:02:42.180
(audience gasping)

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.890
And I wanna do this as much as possible

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:47.193
before he starts flicking
it off all over the place.

00:02:47.193 --> 00:02:48.540
(air whooshing)

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.940
Okay, he did it, nonetheless.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.155
Wow, this is soaked already.

00:02:53.155 --> 00:02:54.150
(water dripping)

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.820
Then I have the next ShamWow dog towel.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.370
These are super absorbent
so they do a great job

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.590
at holding the water and
pulling the water off your dog.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:02.490
Okay, come on.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.157
(fur whooshing)

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:08.850
You see the floor is already
soaked and he just came out.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:09.810
Bear, are you happy?

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.150
Yeah, who's happy?

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.440
Hang out here for a second.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.970
Tell me this doesn't look

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:18.540
like the twin turbo back end of a jet.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.060
You might look at this contraption and say

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.500
to yourself, "Why in the world

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.350
do you need such a crazy dog blower?

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:26.820
Dog skin is too sensitive

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:28.290
so you can't really use heat.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.090
The goal with dogs in drying them,

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.370
especially big floofy dogs like Bear, is

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.242
to blow the wetness off of them.

00:03:35.242 --> 00:03:37.992
(dryer whirring)

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.260
When you blow really forceful air,

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.060
you could actually see his skin

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.040
and that allows me as I go through,

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.630
to see if there's any rashes

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.220
or anything else popping up in his skin.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.900
Also, a mistake that a lot of people make

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.300
with these, if you go in
like circles like this,

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.790
you could actually create
tangles in your dog's hair.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.600
So the goal is to always
do it in one direction.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:07.600
(dryer whirring)
(quirky music)

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.364
Oh, my low back!

00:04:10.364 --> 00:04:13.075
(groans) The tail stays
wagging, right bud?

00:04:13.075 --> 00:04:14.763
The tail's just wagging, yeah.

00:04:14.763 --> 00:04:17.790
This is like a shearing blade, it's a comb

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.620
but on the other end, it's really sharp.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.150
So you're going through his floof,

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:24.570
it could actually take extra
hair out and tangles out.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.460
A lot of dog groomers
will avoid using these

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.810
'cause some people overuse them

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.640
and start like ripping
hair outta their dogs.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.110
So you have to be really conscientious

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.260
about how you use this.

00:04:33.487 --> 00:04:35.347
"Get a newfie," they say.

00:04:35.347 --> 00:04:36.600
"It'd be fun," they say.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.050
When hair clumps together
on a dog like this, oxygen

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.720
and air stops being
able to pass through it.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.430
The dog becomes more vulnerable

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.340
to skin infections, fungal and bacterial.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.370
I had a groomer for about a year

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.350
and then they just started
jacking up their prices

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:56.010
to like $600, even though
this takes only two hours.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:57.150
I mean, they do come to you

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:00.090
but then their scheduling
system was a mess,

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.070
and I actually enjoy doing this.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.240
The only negative part

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.100
about this is, obviously
the hair everywhere

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.960
so you have to vacuum after.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:11.220
And then, also the fact that
my water pressure sucks,

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.470
but otherwise it's great.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:14.910
It's very therapeutic.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.620
It's probably why moms

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.440
or dads braid their children's hair.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.570
It's like it's fun for them.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.280
And you also see that in other primates.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.803
I think monkeys love
grooming each other too.

00:05:26.885 --> 00:05:28.920
I feel like I'm a monkey
right now grooming a bear.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:30.603
Interspecies grooming.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:32.880
Do you think he likes it, though?

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:34.127
Look at this guy (chuckles).

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.920
Drooling.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.393
This is a wire brush.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.750
It's good for finishing his coat

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.220
but I also use it in between

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.620
to sort of get some of
the smaller tangles out

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.210
before I go with the bigger brush.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.950
Didn't he get bigger?

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.840
It's 'cause he gets floofier.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.771
(mellow music)

00:05:54.771 --> 00:05:56.989
(brush clicking)

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:58.050
Just crazy.

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:00.240
Again, whatever thing you use

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.250
on your dog, introduce it to the dog.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.167
Bear hasn't seen this in a little while

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:04.950
'cause I wasn't clipping him so I need him

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:07.080
to be calm when I turn this on,

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.630
turn that on, let him see
that nothing bad happens.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:12.990
And then, basically, I
just wanna clean up the fur

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.970
in between his paws here,

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.351
'cause when it overgrows
it can be a problem.

00:06:18.351 --> 00:06:21.268
(trimmer whirring)

00:06:22.395 --> 00:06:24.270
I'm actually surprised
Bear is so comfortable

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.730
with letting me play
with his paws because,

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.950
when he was a puppy he
actually cut his paw real bad

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:30.810
and I had to take staples out of it

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:34.770
after he got an operation and
he let me do it like a champ.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.330
But it's important when your dog's a puppy

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.580
that you handle their paws regularly

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.430
for this exact reason, so
that you can groom your dog.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:45.990
Here we have a Dremel, which
is how I shorten Bear's nails.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.960
If you actually apply a
slight pressure to the top

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:51.540
of the nail and to the bottom
of the paw pad like this,

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.550
you can express the nail
a little bit further

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.784
which will allow you to
visualize the vein better.

00:06:55.784 --> 00:06:58.617
(Dremel whirring)

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:04.580
Newf, it's time to take
care of your gums and teeth

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:08.640
to make sure that you don't get cavities.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:09.930
Bear is a little annoying

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.280
when brushing his teeth,

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:13.080
'cause he likes to eat the toothbrush.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.200
Okay, so we're gonna get
some of the toothpaste

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.520
on the toothbrush

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.800
and Bear will give you his teeth

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.575
and allow you to brush them.

00:07:21.575 --> 00:07:24.030
(toothbrush grazing)

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:26.130
And he'll eat the toothpaste, like I said.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.520
This is not a glamorous job,

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.410
but it's a job that someone has to do.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.300
The hardest part is
getting the back teeth.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.760
Yeah, I'm getting those back teeth.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:36.750
Don't chew the toothbrush.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:39.450
Just wait, wait before you
chew the toothbrush please.

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:41.310
I actually don't mind
when he chews so much

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:42.143
on the back ones,

00:07:42.143 --> 00:07:44.523
'cause then it's like he's
helping me brush them.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:48.060
Next, we need to clean the inside

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:49.680
of, well, not really the inside,

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.920
more like the outer inside of Bear's ear.

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:55.530
And I have these special
wipes that my vet recommended.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:56.790
They're called Vet's Best.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.560
They have witch hazel, aloe vera

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.980
and tea tree oil, all good
ingredients against infections.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:05.190
The goal is not to go
inside your dog's ear fully,

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:07.710
but just to visualize the
ear and get the gunk out.

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:10.140
Bear gets a lot of gunk in his ears, again

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:13.770
because of his floopiness of his ears.

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:15.030
See how gross it is already?

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.760
I also, sometimes will use a solution

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.560
if there's like a lot of ear wax

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.180
or a lot of buildup that you actually put

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:23.513
into his ear and then let
him shake his ear out.

00:08:23.513 --> 00:08:24.780
Oh, and a lot of people

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.070
don't let their dogs shake their heads

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.180
when they're cleaning their ears.

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.170
Definitely let them, 'cause

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:30.180
that could mean some water got in there

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:32.010
and the way that they
get it out is by shaking.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:34.560
Last part of Bear's grooming routine is

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.140
to get him outside of the
bathroom away from all this hair.

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:37.973
Before we move on

00:08:37.973 --> 00:08:40.816
to the next section, status
check-in of the Bear floof hair.

00:08:40.816 --> 00:08:42.420
(suspenseful music)

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.060
All right, part two, we wanna
get him out of the bathroom

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:47.280
because it's really
wet in there and hairy.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.440
So we wanna do the
finishing touches in here.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.910
He's already coming to join us.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:53.280
All right, newf, we're
gonna finish your coat now

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.630
and blow you out,

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.160
and then I'm gonna do a
little haircut for you

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.930
because you're getting
a little bit too poofy.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:59.045
High-five if that's okay.

00:08:59.045 --> 00:08:59.878
(paw smacking)

00:08:59.878 --> 00:09:00.711
Okay, good.

00:09:00.711 --> 00:09:02.670
(dryer whirring)

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:04.239
Play dead.

00:09:04.239 --> 00:09:06.989
(dryer whirring)

00:09:08.741 --> 00:09:11.130
Not the most glamorous
part of owning a dog,

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:12.420
shaving his (beep).

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:14.790
But, he gets a lot of rashes here

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.757
'cause of the moisture gets trapped.

00:09:16.757 --> 00:09:21.757
(mellow music)
(Bear's heart lub-dubbing)

00:09:22.835 --> 00:09:25.085
Isn't this incredible, Dad?

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.280
Well, how would Bear survive in the wild?

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:30.240
That's my question.

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:33.660
He would get so matted so
quickly on his first day

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:36.977
of being wet, he would get
skin infections galore.

00:09:36.977 --> 00:09:38.047
(Mike chuckling)

00:09:38.047 --> 00:09:39.300
I think this is already more fur

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.770
than what we had in the bathroom.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:44.383
Yeah, this is your favorite
part, I know, I know.

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:48.630
The least glamorous part
of having a dog here,

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.760
he's looking back at me as I do it.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.199
Yeah, clean my butt.

00:09:52.199 --> 00:09:54.060
(scissors clicking)

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:58.320
Gotta keep the back area
hygienic, right, newf?

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:00.240
Look at the shine on this coat.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.280
This is a healthy mammal right here.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:03.348
How do you feel?

00:10:03.348 --> 00:10:04.181
(Bear barking)

00:10:04.181 --> 00:10:05.550
You smell nice.

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:07.920
Mmm, who's happy?

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:08.910
Who's happy?

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:10.650
Come gimme a hug.

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:11.900
Yeah, you're happy, yeah.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.490
Your breath smells nice.

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:16.620
All right, the floof is clean.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:20.007
He's dry for the most part, he's happy.

00:10:20.007 --> 00:10:24.930
Look at how much fur leaves this animal.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.030
And honestly, if I sat here brushing him

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:29.910
for another hour, probably
I could double this.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:32.520
But as you could tell, it's pretty easy

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.190
to groom a dog that behaves well.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:38.130
So it's important to handle
your dog early, get them used

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:40.140
to you being the owner
and playing with them

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.730
and cleaning their ears and their teeth

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:42.690
and their paws,

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:44.970
because then it becomes
a rewarding experience

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:46.110
for the both of you.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:48.022
That's why Bear's a happy pup, right?

00:10:48.022 --> 00:10:48.855
(Bear barking)

00:10:48.855 --> 00:10:49.710
Yeah, good boy.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.980
Check out Bear's video
when I first got him.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:54.030
Click here to check that out.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:56.147
And as always, stay happy and healthy.

00:10:56.147 --> 00:10:57.370
(signal beeping)

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:00.037
(ominous music)

